{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Hermes failure classification, one saved search.

   Five failure classes differ only in their matched string, so classify in
   SPL and suppress per class rather than shipping five near-identical
   searches. Each pattern is the literal text Hermes (or this estate's own
   pinned-source patches to it) actually logs, not a guess at the underlying
   condition:

   - provider_exhausted: cron/scheduler.py's fallback-exhaustion message,
     rewritten by ansible-proxmox-ai's patches_cron_wall_clock.yml
     ("Classify local stops and fallback exhaustion in delivered failures")
     to read "every fallback rung refused the request".
   - cron_wall_clock_timeout: the same patch's wall-clock branch, "exceeded
     its aggregate wall-clock limit".
   - kanban_block_or_stuck: two upstream signals folded into one class --
     the per-profile digest's "Stuck >Nh:" banner
     (roles/hermes_agent/templates/kanban-digest.py.j2::stuck_line) and
     gateway/kanban_watchers.py's "kanban dispatcher stuck: ready queue
     non-empty" warning.
   - slack_api_error: every Slack adapter log line is prefixed "[Slack]"
     (plugins/platforms/slack/adapter.py); paired with an error-ish keyword,
     excluding the adapter's own normal-teardown DEBUG line ("... failed
     while stopping") so healthy shutdown and "[Slack] connected" style
     lines are not swept in.
   - compaction_loop: agent/conversation_loop.py's "Context compression
     failed after N attempts".

   `profile` is not yet a confirmed extracted field at index time (no Cribl
   config in this repo to verify it) -- `stats by ... profile` drops every
   row for events missing that field, so a fillnull backfills it to
   "unknown" before the stats so the class still fires and groups when
   `profile` is absent, and gets more useful the moment that extraction
   lands.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
[hermes_failure_classes]
description = Classifies Hermes failures into five classes from sourcetype=hermes:* content -- provider_exhausted, cron_wall_clock_timeout, kanban_block_or_stuck, slack_api_error, compaction_loop -- and reports counts by host/profile. One search instead of five near-identical ones; see the template header for the exact matched strings and their source.
search = index=hermes sourcetype=hermes:* _index_earliest=-15m _index_latest=now | eval failure_class=case(match(_raw, "every fallback rung refused the request"), "provider_exhausted", match(_raw, "exceeded its aggregate wall-clock limit"), "cron_wall_clock_timeout", match(_raw, "Stuck >") OR match(_raw, "kanban dispatcher stuck"), "kanban_block_or_stuck", match(_raw, "\[Slack\]") AND match(_raw, "(?i)(failed|error|unhealthy)(?!.*while stopping)"), "slack_api_error", match(_raw, "Context compression failed after"), "compaction_loop") | where isnotnull(failure_class) | fillnull value="unknown" profile | stats count by failure_class, host, profile
dispatch.earliest_time = -15m
dispatch.latest_time = now
cron_schedule = */5 * * * *
enableSched = 1
is_visible = 1
disabled = 0
alert.severity = 3
alert.suppress = 1
alert.suppress.period = 240m
alert.suppress.fields = failure_class,host,profile
alert.track = 1
counttype = number of events
relation = greater than
quantity = 0
